          {
            "line": 484,
            "text": "/*"
          },
          {
            "line": 485,
            "text": " * Synchronous API for calling D-Bus in libnm is deprecated. See"
          },
          {
            "line": 486,
            "text": " * https://networkmanager.dev/docs/libnm/latest/usage.html#sync-api"
          },
          {
            "line": 487,
            "text": " *"
          },
          {
            "line": 488,
            "text": " * Note that \"deprecated\" here does not really mean that the API is going"
          },
          {
            "line": 489,
            "text": " * to be removed. We don't break API. Just comment that it is awkward and"
          },
          {
            "line": 490,
            "text": " * discouraged. The user may:"
          },
          {
            "line": 491,
            "text": " *"
          },
          {
            "line": 492,
            "text": " *   - continue to use this API. It's deprecated, awkward and discouraged,"
          },
          {
            "line": 493,
            "text": " *     but if it works for you, that's fine."
          },
          {
            "line": 494,
            "text": " *"
          },
          {
            "line": 495,
            "text": " *   - use asynchronous API. That's the only sensible way to use D-Bus."
          },
          {
            "line": 496,
            "text": " *     If libnm lacks a certain asynchronous counterpart, it should be"
          },
          {
            "line": 497,
            "text": " *     added."
          },
          {
            "line": 498,
            "text": " *"
          },
          {
            "line": 499,
            "text": " *   - use GDBusConnection directly. There really isn't anything wrong"
          },
          {
            "line": 500,
            "text": " *     with D-Bus or GDBusConnection. This deprecated API is just a wrapper"
          },
          {
            "line": 501,
            "text": " *     around g_dbus_connection_call_sync(). You may call it directly"
          },
          {
            "line": 502,
            "text": " *     without feeling dirty."
          },
          {
            "line": 503,
            "text": " *"
          },
          {
            "line": 504,
            "text": " * The API is marked as deprecated since 1.22, however the macro only starts"
          },
          {
            "line": 505,
            "text": " * complaining in 1.24. That's intentional, because in 1.22 the asynchronous"
          },
          {
            "line": 506,
            "text": " * alternative was not yet available."
          },
          {
            "line": 507,
            "text": " */"
          },
          {
            "line": 508,
            "text": "#define _NM_DEPRECATED_SYNC_METHOD             NM_DEPRECATED_IN_1_24"
          },
